# Cocoatree retrieves known results from pySCA

In this folder, we run cocoatree (all co-evolution metrics + all
normalization) on several datasets added to cocoatree (halabi, rivoire, and
rhomboid).

Here are the scripts/results:

    - `run_cocoatree_with_gt.py` loads datasets from cocoatree and runs the
      analysis with the desired metric + correction. It writes results in
      `results/cocoatree_gt/{dataset}/cocoatree_{metric}_{correction}.csv` and
      the coevolution matrix in the same directory / filename but with
      `-distances.csv`

    - `plot_scatter_sectors.py`  plots the results of the IC with sectors colors +
      groundtruth when known.

    - `plot_figure_confusion_matrices.py`  plots the confusion matrix (both
      row and all vs all formats)

All results are generated when typing snakemake -c {njobs}.

The figure_*.py plot the results for the main figures.
